{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/711328-strange-bloodlines","id":711328,"title":"Strange bloodlines","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-20T15:15:10-07:00","id":711328,"title":"Strange bloodlines","content":"We all know that Garou, Mokole, and Bastet shouldn't breed among their own kind because that will result in them creating Metis. But they CAN breed among each other and with other shapeshifters. What might be the effects if they had tried booking up with each other instead of just human and animals? Gurhal that could naturally step sideways? Bastet with Mnesis? Mokole that are as ageless as the Rokea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T15:46:21-07:00","id":711372,"title":"","content":"5% chance of either breed and being kin to the other, remaining 90% of children are kinfolk to both breeds. For female lupus and similar beast-born, there's only a five percent chance for the mother's breed. Kitsune have it even worse, with a higher probability of mortality for both parties in the event of a Kitsune being born as part of the union. It's all covered in, most recently, W20 Changing Breeds. Earlier, it was in the 2nd edition player's guide and revised storyteller's handbook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T19:22:04-07:00","id":711605,"title":"","content":"Whoa, only 5% either way? That seems more punishing than it used to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T22:18:58-07:00","id":711816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/711328-strange-bloodlines?p=711605#post711605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoa, only 5% either way? That seems more punishing than it used to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't let my Garou or Fera mating result in much of anything in my games. This is mainly due to the role of kinfolk in the story- I think having human families is important. Being forced to relate and care for the weak little apes really helps players grow and expand their characters, at least in my experience; you just gotta treat the kinfolk as fleshed-out characters, rather than fucktoys or targets for Wyrm attacks. If the changing breeds can just screw each other and have a better chance of producing shifters that way than with their own kinfolk, things can get out of whack thematically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 10-21-2015, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}